---
import Page from '@layouts/Page.astro';
import Image from 'astro/components/Image.astro';
import portrait from '@assets/img/portrait-bw-2023-12.jpg';
const title = 'About Me';
const description = 'My name is David and I\'m a web developer, technical author and musician from Ireland.';
---

<Page title={ title } description={ description }>

  <Image src={ portrait } alt="David Matthew" class="float-right ml-4 mb-4 w-64 max-w-1/2 p-3 border-2 border-zinc-600" />

  <p>My name is David and I'm a web developer, technical author and musician from Ireland.</p>

  <p>
    I'm always working on one project or another. Being creative is not only a core part of my mental 
    health regimen; it's essentially how I stay sane (in an increasingly dystopic reality). What also helps 
    is that I am an extremely proud papai of a beautiful Brazilian-Irish boy, and an ever-grateful husband to 
    a wonderful wife and mulher maravilhosa.
  </p>

  <h2>Stuff I Do</h2>
  
  <p>
    I have <a href="/generative-art-javascript-svg/">one book to my name</a> so far, on the subject of Generative Art 
    (<strong>not</strong> the AI kind - if you're curious about my views on AI <a href="/tag/ai/">see here</a>). I've 
    released a few EPs and an album with the independent Irish label Inner Chapter Music, and am currently working 
    on a solo piano album.
  </p>

  <p>
    On the code side of things, I created the 
    <a href="https://github.com/davidmatthew-ie/svjs" target="_blank">SvJs JavaScript library</a> 
    for generative artists (which I use for the examples in my book on the same subject), maintain 
    <a href="https://profiles.wordpress.org/davidmatthew/#content-plugins" target="_blank">some WordPress plugins</a> 
    (though I now primarily work in Drupal, Eleventy and Astro - the latter is what this site runs on) and have 
    more recently been focussed on MusicXML and web audio.
  </p>

  <h2>Education</h2>

  <table class="max-w-3xl">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Qualification</th>
        <th>Institution</th>
        <th>Year</th>
        <th>Result</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>MSc Interactive Media</td>
        <td>University College Cork</td>
        <td>2017</td>
        <td>1:1</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>MA Philosophy</td>
        <td>University College Cork</td>
        <td>2007</td>
        <td>1:1</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>BA Philosophy</td>
        <td>University College Dublin</td>
        <td>2006</td>
        <td>2:1</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    My original undergraduate and postgraduate qualifications are in Philosophy - a far-cry from coding! 
    Or superficially so at least. The discipline of deep, abstract thought and the exercise of logic (logic 
    being a core subject of philosophy) are invaluable when it comes to computer programming of any kind. 
    This is especially true now that more and more developers are outsourcing their thinking to statistical
    text extruding machines (otherwise known as Generative AI) which over time can only lead to cognitive decline.
  </p>

</Page>
